WEBVTT

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:18.580
Flamme.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:19.910
You mean "Master."

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:22.870
What is it?

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:26.830
Do you really think it's unfair?

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.720
Frieren, do you remember Basalt's last words?

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.630
No.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.430
Their kind uses words only to deceive humans.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.180
That's right.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.480
They're nothing more than monsters 
capable of speech.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.810
That's the true nature of the 
creatures I call demons.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.950
They don't play fair, 
so we must be even more unfair.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:03.000
If it allows me to exterminate demonkind, 
then I will gladly embrace this dishonor.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.000
Like a fairy tale

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.420
It's a sign the story has reached its end

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.340
Like a single passage taken from

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.970
A journey that was too long

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.300
Of the evil that once cast a shadow

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.640
Across this land

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.970
And the memories of the short journey

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.440
With the hero who defeated it

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:36.200
Beyond Journey's End

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.740
The story ends

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.240
And the hero goes to sleep

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:44.080
Leaving this land with

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.750
Days of peace and quiet

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.250
The passage of time heartlessly

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.420
Makes people forget

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:53.210
Even the tracks left behind by his life

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.010
Begin to rust

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.840
Just the same

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.140
Your words and wishes and courage

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.470
Are still inside of me

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.350
And they live on

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.890
We chose the same path

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:09.020
That's all it was supposed to be

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.560
Why is it that at some point

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.820
I wanted to understand the reason for

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.190
The tears that fall down my cheeks

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.280
Even now

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.660
If I retrace the journey we walked together

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.200
Even though you're not there

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.870
I know I'll be able to find it

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.010
Episode 10: A Powerful Mage

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.770
The bleeding won't stop.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:48.890
This is the end.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.100
Your plan has failed.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.070
You're right.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.860
But Frieren won't escape unscathed.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.240
She must be fighting Lady Aura by now.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:07.120
Previously, we were forced to 
retreat by the party of heroes.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.960
But this time, there are 
no heroes to protect her.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.210
It's true that Frieren is a threat to us,

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.880
but she has far less mana than Lady Aura.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:23.720
If she engages her directly, 
Frieren will lose.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.720
Then Frieren will win.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:32.390
She'd never directly engage a demon.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.060
I know she'll trick Aura and kill her.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:38.070
Nonsense.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:43.910
Frieren the Slayer has always 
engaged us directly.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.290
Why do I feel like something is wrong?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.960
This girl's mana is weak,

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:56.840
and yet I was overwhelmed by the 
sheer number of her rapid attacks.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:02.550
But how was she able to do that 
without exhausting her mana?

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:08.060
I understand now. Is that even possible?

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.310
So Frieren does the same.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.810
What you've done isn't fair.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.650
You're a disgrace to all mages.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.280
Ms. Frieren knows that better than anyone.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.250
What a dreadful sight.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.420
Looks like an elf village.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.520
Basalt the Throne,

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.810
a general of the Demon King's army.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:58.190
He must've led his forces here 
to destroy this village.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.320
Are you the one who killed him? 
You seem nearly dead yourself.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.000
That's a lot of mana.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.460
You must be powerful.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:17.370
Did you engage the demons directly?

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.960
What a fool you are.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:26.550
Why do people always engage 
their enemies directly?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.090
Run, hide, take your enemies by surprise...

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.720
There are plenty of other options.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.310
I'll never understand strong mages.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.480
But you do.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:39.230
What?

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.860
You should understand how I feel...

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:49.950
because you're a far more powerful mage.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.250
What makes you say that?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.260
Just a feeling.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.390
What's your name?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.850
What happened to the village?

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:19.690
Its people are dead, down to 
the last woman and child.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:25.230
I was the strongest, but I still 
couldn't protect them.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.900
You really are a fool.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.280
If I'd been in your shoes, 
I wouldn't have hesitated to run.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:33.830
Put me down.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.290
No.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:38.830
You have potential. 
You're going to be my apprentice.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.710
And you know you wouldn't have survived 
if I hadn't happened upon you.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:50.050
On top of failing to protect the village, 
you nearly died yourself.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.640
Your death truly would've been in vain.

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:56.640
We're being pursued.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:00.520
They're stronger than the general you killed.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.950
Interesting creatures, aren't they?

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.990
They had every intention 
of catching us off guard

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.450
by concealing their mana 
until just before they struck,

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:20.830
but the moment they realized we were mages, 
they stepped out into the open.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.590
They're cunning and they don't play fair,

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:29.300
but every last one of them has a ridiculous 
sense of pride when it comes to magic.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:34.890
Human mage, leave the elf girl and go.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.020
Will you let me go if I do?

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.680
"Kill all the elves."

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.020
Those were the Demon King's orders.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.940
Your life matters not to me.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.730
I see.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:58.160
Frieren, it's true that I'm painfully aware 
of what it's like to be a powerful mage.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:02.290
I know exactly how these creatures feel, too.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:08.170
I know the absolute confidence they 
have in the magics they've studied.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.670
In other words, they're stupidly 
proud and overconfident.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:32.490
Frieren, unlike you, 
they judged me a weakling.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:40.160
Though they were exceptional mages, 
their overconfidence cost them their lives.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:45.210
You hid your strength by controlling 
how much mana you release.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:47.540
That's right.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:52.340
Deceive and kill your enemies by allowing 
them to miscalculate your strength.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:58.470
It's a cowardly and unfair way to fight 
that makes a mockery of magic.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.610
Your injuries are looking a lot better.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.740
Shall we begin your training?

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.500
Flamme.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.000
You mean "Master."

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:33.460
Demons took everything from me.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:34.670
Me, too.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.760
I hate them so much that I wish 
I could exterminate every last one.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.010
Me, too.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.890
But I love magic.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.140
So do I.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:52.900
Which is why only you and I should become 
cowards who make a mockery of magic.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.990
What should I do to train?

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:02.530
Try limiting the mana you release 
to one-tenth of its normal volume.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.790
Impressive. You're controlling it well.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:11.960
Any elf can do this.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:17.090
While you do that, we'll work on your 
fundamentals and raise your base mana level.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.130
That's all?

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.390
Simple, right?

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.520
By the way, how long should 
I keep suppressing my mana?

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:29.190
It starts to get tiring 
if I do it for too long.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.020
As long as I do.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.440
For life.

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.320
You'll spend your entire life fooling demons.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.620
Lügner is dead.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:48.120
Now all your executioners 
have been eliminated.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.250
You've failed, Aura.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.210
You're right. It's a shame.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:57.880
But if I can defeat you here, 
then it won't have been for nothing.

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:05.970
In this battle, you've released numerous 
immortal soldiers from my control.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:11.980
Was it wise to expend so much mana against me?

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.190
The Scales of Obedience.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.320
When two souls are placed on the scale,

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.740
whichever has more mana 
forces the other to submit.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:29.040
Aura can only use such a risky spell 
because of her tremendous amount of mana.

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.330
Generally speaking,

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:34.500
a person's mana increases in proportion 
with the time spent training.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:39.340
I can feel it in the mana pouring off Aura.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:43.510
She's a great demon who has lived 
for over five hundred years,

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:47.010
and she's spent most of her life training.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:49.850
Five hundred years, huh?

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:53.150
That's fairly long-lived for a demon.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:55.360
I doubt she's been challenged before.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:00.530
I can learn so much just from 
the mana flowing off her.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:05.910
Regardless, demons don't conceal 
their mana—nor can they.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.120
A pity.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.540
Auserlese.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.550
Master.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:22.550
Demons are cunning, aren't they?

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:26.680
Why don't they constantly suppress 
their mana like you do?

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:29.430
They can't.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:33.440
Demons are individualists,

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:37.940
but they form the barest connections 
needed to fight against humankind.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.820
What do you think an organization 
needs to function?

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.530
Order?

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:45.450
That's right.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:49.950
In other words, you need someone 
important to lead an organization.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.410
In the case of humans,

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:57.460
importance is determined by status 
and wealth, like they do in this nation.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:02.210
That well-dressed man exiting 
that palace is a man of importance.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:05.340
It's hard to tell which humans are important,

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:09.430
so they dress themselves up 
to make it obvious.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.600
Demons are different?

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:16.520
They haven't changed a bit 
since they were monsters.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.520
Might makes right.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:20.730
It's far easier to understand than humans.

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:23.240
You can tell who's strong 
just by looking at them.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:24.990
You mean mana.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:30.030
Mana is to them what status 
and wealth are for humans.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:32.490
It's dignity itself.

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:38.170
They may temporarily suppress 
their mana for the sake of stealth,

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:42.630
but none are foolish enough 
to suppress their mana all the time.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:47.050
It's the difference between a noble 
sneaking out into town incognito

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:51.390
and that same noble debasing themselves by 
abandoning their status and wealth entirely.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.180
The world of demons is cruel.

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:59.310
They'd never grant any dignity 
to those with little mana.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:04.650
So the stronger they are, the more desperate 
they are to show off their mana.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:10.160
For them, there's no benefit to 
constantly suppressing their mana.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.910
It doesn't even occur to them to do it.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.120
It's a pity, isn't it?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:20.670
Just as humans are bound by status 
and wealth, demons are bound by mana.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:25.460
Despite their pride in 
and unparalleled love for magic,

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:28.300
they can't control their own mana.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.890
Frieren, you're lucky you're not a demon.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:36.180
You're right. I wouldn't be able 
to deceive them if I were.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:44.070
It's been three years since you 
started suppressing your mana.

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:47.440
Looks like I was right about you.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.580
You've grown much better at that.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:00.000
Frieren, do you still love magic?

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:03.540
Where did that come from, Master?

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.210
Somewhat, I suppose.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:11.890
Long ago, you once confidently 
answered that you loved magic.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.390
That was only fifty years ago.

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:17.140
You're right.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:24.150
In the end, all I could do 
was teach you to fight.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:26.400
Magic for revenge.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.110
Do you regret it?

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:34.990
No. I'm glad I taught my magic to you.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.950
Given how long you'll live,

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:42.040
you might eventually become strong 
enough to defeat the Demon King.

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:47.340
Frieren, I have one request.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:48.880
What is it?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:53.300
Plant flowers around my grave.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:55.010
That doesn't seem like you.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:56.180
I know.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:05.020
Frieren, my favorite spell 
creates a field of beautiful flowers.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:09.440
My parents taught it to me when I was little.

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:12.110
It's what made me love magic.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:13.910
Huh.

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:18.160
Teach me that spell.

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:27.880
Listen to me, Frieren.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:31.420
You must never seek to leave 
your name in history.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:33.800
Live in obscurity.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:39.760
You won't leave your name in history 
until you defeat the Demon King.

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:43.700
I've heard there's a long-lived 
mage in these woods.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.580
Are you her?

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:50.590
I've lived a long time, but I haven't 
done much with my life.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:53.710
I'm not exceptional.

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:57.220
Huh. What do you think, Heiter?

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:01.850
She has roughly one-fifth of my mana.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.220
It's not bad.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.100
Who's this irritating guy?

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:10.560
Leave. You don't have business 
with a mediocre mage, do you?

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:15.240
No, you're stronger than 
any mage I've ever met.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.240
What makes you say that?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.910
Just a feeling.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.460
Auserlese.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:48.850
You seem happy, Aura.

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.100
Are you certain you'll win?

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:54.110
You'll see.

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:56.860
Frieren the Slayer.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:01.820
You made your first major 
appearance eighty years ago.

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:05.620
With the party of heroes, 
you defeated the Demon King.

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:09.330
You're a mysterious elven mage 
whose age is unknown.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:15.460
But it doesn't matter how 
long-lived a mage you are.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.340
Your mana tells me everything 
I need to know.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.800
I can see it quite clearly.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:27.430
You're an exceptional mage, 
but your mana itself is unimpressive.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:32.150
You can't have had more than a 
hundred years or so of training.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:35.570
Not only that, but you've barely 
changed since eighty years ago.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:39.280
Were you honing other skills 
instead of working on your mana?

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:42.070
Or were you simply wasting your life away?

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:47.580
Either way, you are no match for me.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.840
I win.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:06.350
All that's left is to sever your head myself.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:14.690
It wasn't even necessary 
to exhaust Frieren's mana.

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.360
I needn't have been so cautious.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:20.990
She defeated many of my 
immortal soldiers, too.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:22.740
I'll have to replenish their numbers later.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.240
What's this?

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.410
The scales are starting to tip toward Frieren.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:35.630
You placed my soul on the scales, Aura.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:41.460
Honestly, I would've been in trouble 
if you'd tried to overwhelm me with numbers.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:45.390
I'm glad you're so confident in your own mana.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:48.100
Now I can finally defeat you.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.520
What do you mean?

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.020
You should've figured it out by now.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.020
I've been suppressing my mana.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.520
You misjudged the situation, Aura.

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:06.160
That's impossible. That wouldn't 
have escaped my notice.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:10.740
There was no hint of the instability 
or variation in mana output

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:12.290
that comes with suppression.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:17.960
I'm surprised. Demons are capable 
of observing mana that precisely?

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:21.550
Sounds like my master made the 
right call with her methods.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:27.180
I've spent most of my life 
suppressing my mana.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:29.390
This state has become natural for me.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:35.060
Are you stupid? Why would you 
do something so pointless?

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:37.940
You're right. It's stupid.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.690
But it lets me beat your kind.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:45.950
This is absurd.

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:49.200
I'm a great demon who's lived 
for over five hundred years.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:54.370
Aura, the person standing before you...

00:21:57.500 --> 00:22:00.630
is a mage who's lived 
for over a thousand years.

00:22:14.310 --> 00:22:15.520
Frieren.

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:19.270
Just as demons deceive humankind with words,

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:23.020
you must use your mana to deceive demons.

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.030
Aura,

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:27.280
kill yourself.

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.750
Impossible.

00:22:38.700 --> 00:22:41.380
H-How could I...?

00:22:50.050 --> 00:22:52.600
And you alright

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:55.100
Can you hear me

00:22:55.890 --> 00:23:01.980
Trailing along deserted train tracks

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:04.320
Crying excessively

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:07.490
Wanting you to smile

00:23:07.490 --> 00:23:13.530
I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:17.250
There's something I'd like to tell you

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:20.000
With words more precious than a goodbye

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:25.670
Unremarkable yet special

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:29.220
See, things that couldn't have been

00:23:29.220 --> 00:23:32.260
Seen if it weren't for these eyes

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:37.010
Why? They begin to overflow

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:43.100
So, if I were to be born again

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:48.940
I would surely choose this place once more

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:54.950
So, if we were to meet again

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:00.710
I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:03.670
Even if no promises were made

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:06.590
Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:12.760
Those tears will be alright, 
dawn will surely break

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:15.430
I'm whispering our lullaby

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:19.350
for you to come back home

00:24:20.220 --> 00:24:22.890
Do you have someone to praise you?

00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:22.890
You're traveling to heaven, then?

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:23.060
I'm not sure I understand.

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:24.690
You've got a nice body, old man.

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:26.190
The largest magical city in the 
northern lands, Äußerst.

00:24:24.400 --> 00:24:26.020
What's a first-class mage?

00:24:25.060 --> 00:24:27.150
What is that antique?

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:27.900
I mean that we're elves.

00:24:27.570 --> 00:24:30.030
Episode 11







Winter in the Northern Lands

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:30.070
It was the winters of the northern lands.
